<!--Render Target Documentation — Customizer
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.Customizer-->
<rdoc:Customizer xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    OpenSCAD customizer section
  </is>
  <documentation>
    The customizer generator writes the OpenSCAD customizer section for block
    and set files.

    For each exposed property:

    - Variable declaration with default value
    - Inline comment with customizer dropdown syntax where it applies
    - Group comment /* [Group Name] */ for property groups

    The hidden section /* [Hidden] */ holds derived variables that combine
    customizer inputs before they are passed to the module. Internal module
    computations are never placed in the hidden section.

    OpenSCAD customizer supports only flat primitives. The processor splits
    complex properties into several customizer variables and recombines them in
    [Hidden]. Splitting follows NativeBlock type metadata and annotations.

    split [x, y, z] — a vector becomes named scalars:

        baseRoundingRadiusX = 0.5; // [0:0.1:2]
        baseRoundingRadiusY = 0.5;
        baseRoundingRadiusZ = 0.5;
        /* [Hidden] */
        baseRoundingRadius = [baseRoundingRadiusX, baseRoundingRadiusY, baseRoundingRadiusZ];

    auto_toggle true — a NoneOr value becomes a boolean plus a value:

        recessDepthAuto = true;
        recessDepth = 0.5;
        /* [Hidden] */
        recessDepthResolved = recessDepthAuto ? "auto" : recessDepth;

    suggestions — a dropdown comment from the property suggestions. Each
    suggestion instance is serialized to its SCAD literal:

        textColor = "#303D4E"; // [#303D4E, #EAC645, #58B99D]

    Optional labels may come from documentation on the suggestion instances.

    constraints — Min and Max map to customizer range metadata
    [min:step:max] when both bounds exist. See the BlockML constraints
    documentation for the constraint instances. Individual constraints may also
    inform editor range hints.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:Presets" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:Customizer>
